{"analytical_evaluation": "Analytical evaluation is a method that assesses the performance of algorithms based on theoretical knowledge rather than through experiments or specific applications. It is typically employed when there are significant differences in computational complexity or operational speed between algorithms.|Here is another description: Analytical evaluation is a method of direct assessment that focuses on the theoretical performance of algorithms rather than practical implementation. It is typically employed when there are significant differences in computational complexity or operational speed between algorithms.|Here is another description: Analytical evaluation is a method of direct assessment that evaluates algorithms without conducting experiments or specific applications. It is typically employed when there are significant differences in computational complexity or operational speed between algorithms.|Here is another description: Analytical evaluation is a method of direct assessment that evaluates the performance of an algorithm based on theoretical knowledge rather than through experiments or specific applications. It is categorized into quantitative and qualitative assessments."},
