{"empirical_evaluation": "Empirical evaluation is a method used to assess algorithms by conducting specific operations to gather quantitative data. It is widely recognized for its high accuracy and precision in evaluating algorithmic performance.|Here is another description: Empirical evaluation is a method of indirectly assessing algorithms by using specific operations to quantitatively evaluate their performance. It is currently the most widely used assessment method due to its practical approach.|Here is another description: Empirical evaluation is an indirect method used to quantitatively assess algorithms by employing specific operations. It is categorized into supervised and unsupervised assessments based on the need for a reference image."},
