{"visual_or_qualitative_assessments": "Visual or qualitative assessments are methods of evaluation that depend on the subjective judgment of human evaluators, rather than on quantitative or objective measures."},
{"subjective_assessment_scores": "Subjective assessment scores refer to the evaluations given by human evaluators based on their personal criteria and perceptions. These scores are inherently subjective and can differ significantly from one evaluator to another."},
{"subjective_assessment_scores__vary__greatly": "The predicate 'vary' indicates the degree of difference or inconsistency in the subjective assessment scores provided by different human evaluators. It highlights the lack of uniformity and the potential for wide-ranging evaluations."},
{"greatly": "The object 'greatly' emphasizes the significant extent to which the subjective assessment scores can differ. This underscores the challenges and complexities involved in relying on human evaluations for assessing the quality of segmented images.|Here is another description: The object \"greatly\" emphasizes the extent to which the application of supervised evaluation methods is constrained. It suggests that these limitations are significant enough to severely impact the usability and effectiveness of supervised methods in practical applications."},
{"each_evaluator": "Each evaluator refers to individual human assessors involved in the subjective assessment of image segmentation quality. These evaluators bring their own perspectives and experiences to the evaluation process."},
