{"his_her_own_unique_criteria": "His/her own unique criteria refers to the distinct set of standards or benchmarks that each evaluator uses to judge the quality of segmented images. These criteria are personalized and can vary significantly from one evaluator to another, contributing to the subjective nature of the assessment."},
{"criteria": "Criteria refer to the standards or benchmarks used by human evaluators to judge the quality of segmented images. These criteria are subjective and can vary significantly from one evaluator to another."},
{"criteria__assess__the_quality_of_the_segmented_image": "Assess in this context means to evaluate or judge the quality of the segmented image based on the subjective criteria of the evaluator. This process involves a visual assessment and can vary greatly depending on the evaluator's unique standards."},
