{"direct_evaluation": "Direct evaluation refers to the process of assessing the performance and quality of a segmentation algorithm by directly analyzing its inherent characteristics and metrics.|Here is another description: Direct evaluation refers to methods that assess the performance of algorithms through direct means, such as theoretical analysis, without relying on experimental data or specific applications. It contrasts with indirect methods like empirical evaluation, which use specific operations to quantitatively evaluate algorithms."},
