{"objective_measurement__is_required__independent_of_the_specific_computer": "The phrase 'is required' indicates a necessity or a mandatory condition. In this context, it emphasizes that for the evaluation of segmentation algorithms to be reliable and comparable, the measurement method must be independent of the specific computer used."},
{"independent_of_the_specific_computer": "Being 'independent of the specific computer' means that the measurement or evaluation criteria applied to the segmentation algorithm should yield the same results regardless of the hardware or computational environment in which the algorithm is executed. This ensures that the performance assessment is unbiased and universally applicable."},
{"nowadays": "Nowadays, the evaluation of algorithms has evolved to consider more comprehensive factors beyond just computation time. This modern approach takes into account various aspects to assess the effectiveness and efficiency of algorithms."},
