{"cnn_based_segmentation_method": "The CNN-based segmentation method is a technique that utilizes Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) to perform image segmentation tasks. It involves training a CNN to recognize and delineate different objects or regions within an image, based on the input data provided."},
{"cnn_based_segmentation_method__has_shown__superior_performance": "The predicate \"has shown\" indicates that empirical evidence or experimental results have demonstrated the effectiveness or superiority of the CNN-based segmentation method in comparison to other methods. This suggests that the method has been tested and validated through various studies or applications."},
{"superior_performance": "Superior performance refers to the CNN-based segmentation method's ability to achieve better results or higher accuracy in segmenting images compared to traditional or alternative methods. This could include metrics such as precision, recall, F1 score, or other relevant evaluation criteria that indicate the method's effectiveness in correctly identifying and delineating objects within images."},
