{"a_new_method_based_on_sampling_theory_to_calculate_the_difference_between_automatic_segmentation_and_ground_truth_to_evaluate_the_three_dimensional_segmentation_algorithm": "The new method proposed by Arhid et al. (2016) is based on sampling theory and is designed to calculate the difference between automatic segmentation results and the ground truth. This method aims to evaluate the performance of three-dimensional segmentation algorithms by quantifying the discrepancy between the automated segmentation output and the manually verified ground truth data."},
{"shi_et_al_2014_2015": "Shi et al. (2014, 2015) refers to the work of researchers Shi and colleagues in the years 2014 and 2015, who contributed to the field of image segmentation evaluation."},
