{"the_proposed_method": "The proposed method refers to the formalization technique introduced by Taha et al. in 2014, which aims to select the most appropriate metric for image segmentation based on segmented data and the target of the segmentation task.|Here is another description: The proposed method refers to a systematic approach developed by Peng and Varshney (2015) for evaluating the lower bound in the statistical estimation framework, specifically using the segmentation algorithm Mean Square Error (MSE) as an example.|Here is another description: The proposed method refers to a systematic approach developed by Peng and Varshney (2015) for evaluating the performance of segmentation algorithms within a statistical estimation framework. This method is designed to be effective and robust, providing a benchmark for assessing the accuracy and efficiency of segmentation algorithms, particularly in complex scenarios such as the segmentation of blood vessels in Computed Tomography Angiography (CTA) images."},
