{"ge": "GE is a novel evaluation criterion proposed by Habba et al. in 2018, designed to assess the combination of regions in a segmented image and measure pixel uniformity within each region.|Here is another description: GE, or Gini-Entropy, is a novel evaluation criterion proposed by Habba et al. in 2018. It is designed to assess the combination of regions arrangement in a segmented image and measures pixel uniformity within each region by integrating the Gini index with entropy.|Here is another description: GE is a novel evaluation criterion proposed by Habba et al. in 2018, which combines the Gini index with entropy to evaluate segmented images. It is designed to overcome the limitations of the Gini index alone.|Here is another description: GE is a novel evaluation criterion proposed by Habba et al. in 2018, which combines the Gini index with entropy to evaluate the arrangement of regions in a segmented image.|Here is another description: GE is a variable or term in an equation, representing a specific value or quantity."},
{"ge__combines__the_gini_index_with_entropy": "The predicate \"combines\" indicates that GE integrates two distinct measures\u2014the Gini index and entropy\u2014into a single evaluation criterion to enhance the assessment of segmented images."},
