{"quantitative_assessment_methods": "Quantitative assessment methods are techniques used to evaluate and measure various aspects of a system or process in a numerical or statistical manner. These methods aim to provide objective and consistent results, reducing the influence of subjective factors."},
{"quantitative_assessment_methods__relies_on__visual_quality_judgment": "The phrase \"relies on\" indicates a dependency or requirement of one element on another. In this context, it signifies that quantitative assessment methods depend on or necessitate the use of visual quality judgment to function effectively."},
{"visual_quality_judgment": "Visual quality judgment refers to the subjective evaluation of the quality or performance of a system or process based on visual inspection or observation. It involves assessing aspects such as clarity, contrast, color accuracy, and overall visual appeal, often relying on human perception and interpretation.|Here is another description: Visual quality judgment refers to the process of assessing the quality of visual data, such as images or videos, based on human perception. It is commonly used in various applications, including image segmentation evaluation."},
