{"subjective_evaluation_method": "The subjective evaluation method is a technique that relies on human visual judgment to assess the quality of image segmentation. It is commonly used but has limitations due to its instability and difficulty in providing quantitative descriptions.|Here is another description: The subjective evaluation method is a technique that relies on visual quality judgment by human observers to compare different segmentation result images. It is commonly used in various applications where quantitative assessment is needed.|Here is another description: The subjective evaluation method is a technique that relies on human visual judgment to assess the quality of segmentation results. It involves comparing different segmentation images through the human eye."},
