{"different_segmentation_result_images": "Different segmentation result images are the outputs generated by various image segmentation algorithms. These images are compared using the subjective evaluation method to determine their quality and effectiveness in segmenting the image into meaningful regions."},
{"subjective_evaluation_method__has__poor_stability": "The predicate \"has\" in this context indicates that the subjective evaluation method possesses or is characterized by a certain attribute, which in this case is poor stability."},
{"poor_stability": "Poor stability in the context of the subjective evaluation method refers to the inconsistency and variability in the results obtained when different observers or the same observer at different times evaluates the same segmentation results. This lack of stability makes it difficult to describe the method quantitatively and limits its application."},
{"subjective_evaluation_method__is__difficult_to_describe_quantitatively": "The predicate 'is' indicates a state or characteristic of the subjective evaluation method, specifically highlighting its inherent difficulty in being quantitatively described."},
