{"more_impartial_and_accurate": "Being more impartial and accurate means that objective evaluation methods provide a consistent and reliable assessment of segmentation results, free from the biases and inconsistencies that can arise from human judgment in subjective evaluations."},
{"objective_evaluation__is_not_influenced_by__human_factors": "The phrase \"is not influenced by\" indicates that the objective evaluation method operates independently of external factors, ensuring that the assessment remains unbiased and consistent across different evaluations."},
{"human_factors": "Human factors encompass the subjective judgments, biases, and inconsistencies that can arise when humans are involved in the evaluation process. These factors can lead to variability and instability in assessment results."},
{"khan_and_bhuiyan": "Khan and Bhuiyan are researchers who have contributed to the field of image segmentation evaluation by developing novel methods. Their work focuses on creating objective evaluation techniques that can replace subjective human judgment in assessing segmentation quality."},
{"khan_and_bhuiyan__proposed__weighted_self_entropy_and_weighted_mutual_entropy_segmentation_evaluation_method": "The predicate \"proposed\" indicates that Khan and Bhuiyan introduced or put forward a new method or idea in the context of image segmentation evaluation. This action signifies their contribution to the field by suggesting a novel approach to address existing challenges."},
{"weighted_self_entropy_and_weighted_mutual_entropy_segmentation_evaluation_method": "The weighted self-entropy and weighted mutual entropy segmentation evaluation method is an objective technique proposed by Khan and Bhuiyan. This method measures the heterogeneity of pixels between regions and the homogeneity within regions, providing a quantitative and unbiased assessment of segmentation quality.|Here is another description: The weighted self-entropy and weighted mutual entropy segmentation evaluation method is an objective technique proposed by Khan and Bhuiyan in 2014 and 2011 to assess image segmentation results. This method aims to provide a quantitative and unbiased evaluation of segmentation quality.|Here is another description: The weighted self-entropy and weighted mutual entropy segmentation evaluation method is an objective technique proposed by Khan and Bhuiyan in 2014 and 2011. It aims to measure the heterogeneity of pixels between regions and the homogeneity within regions, providing a quantitative and unbiased assessment of image segmentation."},
{"weighted_self_entropy_and_weighted_mutual_entropy_segmentation_evaluation_method__measures__heterogeneity_of_pixels_between_regions_and_homogeneity_within_the_region": "The predicate \"measures\" indicates that the weighted self-entropy and weighted mutual entropy segmentation evaluation method quantifies specific characteristics of the segmentation results. It assesses the degree to which pixels differ between regions and how uniform they are within a single region."},
{"heterogeneity_of_pixels_between_regions_and_homogeneity_within_the_region": "The heterogeneity of pixels between regions refers to the variation and differences in pixel values across different segmented areas, while homogeneity within the region describes the uniformity and similarity of pixel values within a single segmented area. These metrics are crucial for evaluating the effectiveness and accuracy of image segmentation techniques."},
{"weighted_self_entropy_and_weighted_mutual_entropy_segmentation_evaluation_method__is__easy_to_implement": "The term \"is\" in this context signifies the characteristic or attribute of the weighted self-entropy and weighted mutual entropy segmentation evaluation method. Specifically, it highlights that the method possesses the quality of being easy to implement."},
