{"lu_et_al": "Lu et al. refers to a group of researchers who contributed to the field of image segmentation evaluation. Their work focused on developing methods to objectively assess the quality of image segmentation, particularly by introducing novel approaches that consider the application-specific requirements of segmentation.|Here is another description: Lu et al. refers to a group of researchers who contributed to the field of image segmentation evaluation. Their work focused on developing methods to objectively assess the quality of image segmentation, moving beyond subjective human judgment.|Here is another description: Lu et al. refers to a group of researchers who have contributed to the field of image segmentation evaluation. Their work focuses on developing methods that can objectively assess the quality of image segmentation, moving away from subjective human judgment."},
{"lu_et_al__believed__the_quality_of_segmentation_depends_on_the_application": "The predicate 'believed' indicates that Lu et al. held a particular viewpoint or opinion regarding the evaluation of image segmentation quality. This belief influenced their approach to developing segmentation assessment methods, emphasizing the importance of considering the application context in evaluating segmentation quality."},
{"the_quality_of_segmentation_depends_on_the_application": "The object 'the quality of segmentation depends on the application' encapsulates the core belief of Lu et al. regarding image segmentation. They posited that the effectiveness and quality of segmentation techniques are not universally applicable but are instead contingent upon the specific requirements and context of the application for which the segmentation is intended."},
{"lu_et_al__introduced__target_scale_into_the_evaluation_model_to_constrain_the_relative_segmentation_quality": "The term 'introduced' in this context signifies that Lu et al. incorporated or added a new element or concept into an existing framework or model. Specifically, they introduced a novel approach to improve the evaluation of image segmentation quality."},
