{"to_evaluate_segmentation_quality": "To evaluate segmentation quality means to assess the effectiveness and accuracy of the segmentation process in remote sensing images, ensuring that the segmented regions accurately represent the real-world features they are intended to depict."},
{"marpu_et_al": "Marpu et al. refers to a group of researchers who conducted a study in 2010 focused on improving the evaluation of remote sensing image segmentation quality.|Here is another description: Marpu et al. are researchers who contributed to the field of remote sensing image segmentation by defining specific cases of segmentation errors and proposing new evaluation criteria."},
