{"case_of_over_segmentation_and_under_segmentation": "The case of over-segmentation and under-segmentation refers to common issues in image segmentation where the algorithm either divides an image into too many segments (over-segmentation) or too few segments (under-segmentation), impacting the accuracy and effectiveness of the segmentation process."},
{"marpu_et_al__proposed__corresponding_evaluation_criteria_according_to_the_definition": "The predicate 'proposed' indicates that Marpu et al. put forward or suggested new evaluation criteria as a solution to assess the quality of remote sensing image segmentation, specifically addressing over-segmentation and under-segmentation issues."},
{"corresponding_evaluation_criteria_according_to_the_definition": "The corresponding evaluation criteria according to the definition refer to the specific metrics or standards that Marpu et al. developed to evaluate the quality of segmentation results in remote sensing images, based on their defined cases of over-segmentation and under-segmentation."},
{"this_method__is_to_deal_with__result_of_multi_level_segmentation_algorithm_commonly_used_in_geographic_object_based_image_analysis_geobia": "The phrase \"is to deal with\" indicates the purpose or function of the subject. In this case, the method is specifically intended to address or manage the outcomes produced by a certain algorithm used in Geographic Object-Based Image Analysis (GEOBIA)."},
