{"zhang_et_al__proposed__region_based_precision_and_recall": "The predicate 'proposed' indicates that Zhang et al. introduced or put forward a new concept, method, or idea within their research. In this context, it signifies that they suggested a novel approach to evaluate the quality of image segmentation."},
{"region_based_precision_and_recall": "Region-based precision and recall are metrics proposed by Zhang et al. to evaluate the quality of image segmentation. These metrics assess how well the segmented regions match the actual regions in an image, combining aspects of both precision (the ratio of correctly segmented regions to the total segmented regions) and recall (the ratio of correctly segmented regions to the total actual regions)."},
