{"the_over_segmentation_errors_of_the_i_th_reference_segmentation_object": "The over-segmentation errors of the i-th reference segmentation object refer to the inaccuracies that occur when a segmentation algorithm divides an image into more segments than necessary. This specific error is associated with the i-th reference segmentation object, indicating it is being evaluated or measured in the context of a series or set of segmentation objects."},
