{"qp_method": "The _Qp_ method is a technique used for image segmentation evaluation that involves combining multiple reference images to create a ground truth image.|Here is another description: The _Qp_ method is a technique used for constructing a ground truth image by integrating information from multiple reference images, enhancing the accuracy of segmentation evaluations.|Here is another description: The _Qp_ method is a technique used in the context of image segmentation experiments, specifically for making judgments on the quality of segmentation results."},
{"qp_method__has_advantage__construction_of_ground_truth_combining_different_reference_images": "The predicate \"has_advantage\" indicates that the _Qp_ method offers a specific benefit or improvement over other methods, particularly in the way it constructs the ground truth image."},
{"construction_of_ground_truth_combining_different_reference_images": "The construction of ground truth combining different reference images refers to the process where the _Qp_ method integrates various reference images to form a comprehensive and accurate standard image, enhancing the evaluation of segmentation methods."},
{"ground_truth__combines__different_reference_images": "The predicate \"combines\" describes the process by which the ground truth is created. It involves integrating or merging various elements to form a unified standard. In this context, it specifically refers to the combination of different reference images to construct the ground truth."},
{"different_reference_images": "Different reference images are individual images used as references in the process of creating the ground truth. These images are selected and combined to form a final standard image that serves as a benchmark for evaluating the performance of image segmentation methods."},
{"final_standard_image": "The final standard image is a composite image created through a specific method, which in this context is the _Qp_ method. It serves as a benchmark for evaluating the performance of other methods, such as the Compression-based Texture Merging (CTM) method and the mean-shift method."},
{"final_standard_image__formed_by__combining_different_reference_images": "The predicate \"formed_by\" indicates the process or method through which the final standard image is created. In this case, it refers to the combination of different reference images to produce the final standard image."},
{"combining_different_reference_images": "Combining different reference images involves selecting and merging the best parts of multiple segmentation reference images. This process aims to create a more accurate and comprehensive standard image for evaluation purposes."},
{"single_image": "A single image refers to one individual image used in a process or evaluation. In the context of image segmentation and evaluation, a single image might be considered for use as a reference or standard."},
{"single_image__not_used_as__sole_reference": "The relation \"not_used_as\" indicates that the subject (a single image) is not employed or utilized in a certain capacity or role. Specifically, it suggests that a single image is not used in the role or function described by the object."},
{"sole_reference": "\"Sole reference\" describes the role or function where a single image would be the only or primary image used as a benchmark or standard for comparison or evaluation in a process, such as image segmentation."},
{"figure_h": "Figure h is a composite image created through a specific method that integrates multiple reference images to form a standard for evaluation.|Here is another description: Figure h is a composite image created by the _Qp_ method, which combines human segmentation reference images d-g with figure b. It represents a synthesized standard image used for evaluation purposes."},
{"figure_h__obtained_by__combining_human_segmentation_reference_images_d_g_with_figure_b_using_qp_method": "The predicate \"obtained_by\" describes the process through which figure h was created, involving the combination of several images using a particular method."},
{"combining_human_segmentation_reference_images_d_g_with_figure_b_using_qp_method": "The object describes the process of combining human segmentation reference images d-g with figure b using the _Qp_ method to create figure h. This method involves selecting and merging the best parts of multiple segmentations to form a more accurate standard image for evaluation."},
{"figure_i": "Figure i is a composite image generated through a specific method that evaluates the performance of different image processing techniques. It serves as a reference image in the evaluation of the mean-shift method.|Here is another description: Figure i is a composite image created by combining human segmentation reference images d-g with figure c using the _Qp_ method. It serves as a reference for evaluating image segmentation algorithms."},
{"figure_i__obtained_by__combining_figure_d_g_with_figure_c": "The predicate 'obtained_by' signifies the process or method through which figure i was created. In this context, it refers to the combination of multiple reference images using a specified technique to form a final composite image."},
{"combining_figure_d_g_with_figure_c": "Combining figure d-g with figure c represents the specific method and images used to create figure i. Figures d-g are human segmentation reference images, and figure c is another reference image. Their combination, using the _Qp_ method, results in figure i, which is utilized as a reference for evaluating the mean-shift method."},
{"general_evaluation_algorithm": "The general evaluation algorithm is a method used to determine a standard image by assessing multiple reference images."},
{"general_evaluation_algorithm__selects__best_picture_from_d_g_as_standard_picture": "The predicate \"selects\" indicates the action performed by the general evaluation algorithm, which involves choosing the most appropriate image from a set of options."},
