{"under_segmentation": "'Under-segmentation' refers to a type of segmentation error where the resulting segments are fewer than desired, leading to a loss of detail or important features in the image. In the context provided, under-segmentation is one of the categories used to classify segmentation results based on their F-score values.|Here is another description: The object 'under-segmentation' describes a type of error in image segmentation where the segmentation result contains fewer segments than the ground truth. This can lead to a lower F-score value as it indicates that the segmentation is not detailed enough, missing some of the true segments present in the image."},
