{"unsupervised_evaluation_method__is_a_low_level_data_driven_evaluation_method_based_on__image_features": "The unsupervised evaluation method is characterized as a low-level, data-driven approach. This means it operates based on the intrinsic features extracted directly from the images themselves, rather than relying on external benchmarks or human input."},
{"image_features": "Image features refer to the measurable properties and characteristics derived from images, such as edges, textures, colors, and shapes. These features serve as the foundational data upon which the unsupervised evaluation method relies to make assessments."},
