{"segmentation_result__can_be_evaluated_in_order_from__simple_to_complex": "The phrase \"can be evaluated in order from\" indicates a structured approach to assessing the quality or accuracy of segmentation results. This evaluation process involves a sequence of methods, starting from the simplest and progressing to more complex techniques, to ensure a comprehensive assessment of the segmentation outcome."},
{"simple_to_complex": "The evaluation order \"simple to complex\" refers to a methodical approach where segmentation results are first assessed using basic, straightforward methods, such as visual inspection (analytical method), followed by more sophisticated, unsupervised techniques, and finally, the most rigorous, supervised methods that require standard reference images. This progression ensures that the evaluation is thorough and tailored to the specific requirements of the application."},
