{"for_evaluation": "Evaluation in this context refers to the process of assessing the quality and accuracy of image segmentation results. It involves determining how well the segmentation aligns with the expected or desired outcomes, often using various metrics and methods.|Here is another description: The term \"for evaluation\" refers to the purpose of using the unsupervised evaluation method, which is to assess the quality of image segmentation results. This method is particularly useful in applications where accuracy requirements are not extremely high and standard images are difficult to obtain.|Here is another description: The term \"for evaluation\" refers to the purpose of using the supervised evaluation method, which is to assess the quality and accuracy of image segmentation results. This evaluation is crucial for determining the effectiveness of segmentation algorithms in various applications."},
