{"the_advanced_information_of_the_image_such_as_semantic_information": "The advanced information of the image such as semantic information refers to higher-level data derived from images that go beyond basic pixel values, including context, meaning, and relationships between objects within the image. This can include understanding the overall structure, content, and intended segmentation outcomes as perceived by humans."},
{"evaluation_method": "The evaluation method refers to the techniques and criteria used to assess the quality and accuracy of image segmentation results. It is crucial for comparing different segmentation algorithms, selecting optimal parameters, and developing new segmentation techniques.|Here is another description: The evaluation method refers to the process or technique used to assess the quality or effectiveness of image segmentation results. It can vary depending on the specific application and the type of images being segmented."},
{"evaluation_method__may_obtain_a_more_accurate_understanding_of_the_segmentation_result_image__by_combining_the_overall_frame_information": "The phrase \"may obtain a more accurate understanding of the segmentation result image\" describes the potential enhancement in the assessment process. By integrating advanced image information, such as semantic details and overall frame context, the evaluation method can provide a deeper and more precise analysis of the segmentation outcomes."},
{"by_combining_the_overall_frame_information": "Combining the overall frame information involves using the comprehensive description of an image's content to improve the evaluation process. This approach aims to leverage the contextual and semantic aspects of the image to achieve a more accurate and reliable assessment of the segmentation results."},
