{"three_types_of_deep_neural_networks_for_target_segmentation_evaluation": "The object \"three types of deep neural networks for target segmentation evaluation\" describes the specific contribution made by Huang et al. They proposed three distinct deep neural network architectures designed to automatically learn and evaluate the quality of image segmentations. These networks utilize different strategies such as using segmented objects as input, predicting foreground masks, and extracting features from weighted mask layers."},
{"first_network": "The first network is a type of deep neural network designed for segmentation evaluation. It is part of a set of networks proposed by Huang et al. (2016) to automatically learn deep features for target segmentation evaluation."},
