{"the_number_of_people_participating_in_the_assessment_experiment_reaches_a_certain_amount": "The number of people participating in the assessment experiment reaching a certain amount signifies a threshold where collective human judgment, despite its subjective biases, converges to provide a more reliable and accurate evaluation of segmentation results."},
{"human_assessment": "Human assessment refers to the process where people use their vision to evaluate the quality of natural image segmentation results. This method is labor-intensive and requires a significant number of participants to achieve reliable results."},
{"human_assessment__has__subjective_bias_to_some_extent": "The predicate \"has\" in this context indicates the presence or inclusion of a certain characteristic or attribute within the subject. Here, it signifies that human assessment includes or is characterized by a particular trait."},
{"subjective_bias_to_some_extent": "Subjective bias to some extent refers to the inherent tendency of human evaluators to be influenced by personal experiences, emotions, and life circumstances when assessing natural image segmentation results. This bias can lead to variations in judgment, especially for segmentations that appear very similar."},
{"assessment_results": "Assessment results refer to the outcomes or evaluations derived from a process of examining or judging something, in this case, the quality of natural image segmentation. These results are crucial as they provide insights into the effectiveness and accuracy of the segmentation techniques used."},
{"assessment_results__are_influenced_by__personal_experiences_life_and_emotions": "The phrase \"are influenced by\" indicates a causal relationship where certain factors have an effect on the assessment results. This suggests that the outcomes are not solely objective but are also shaped by various subjective elements."},
{"personal_experiences_life_and_emotions": "Personal experiences, life, and emotions encompass the individual background, past encounters, and emotional states of the assessors. These factors introduce a layer of subjectivity into the assessment process, meaning that different assessors may reach varying conclusions based on their unique perspectives and feelings."},
{"people__can_t_make__accurate_judgments_on_segmentation_results_that_look_very_similar": "The predicate \"can\u2019t make\" indicates a limitation or inability of people to perform a specific task accurately. In this context, it highlights the difficulty people face when trying to evaluate segmentation results that are very similar."},
{"accurate_judgments_on_segmentation_results_that_look_very_similar": "Accurate judgments on segmentation results that look very similar refer to the precise evaluation of natural image segmentation outcomes where the differences between segments are minimal. These judgments are challenging for people due to the subtle distinctions and potential for subjective bias."},
