{"dice": "Dice refers to the Dice coefficient, a statistical measure used to gauge the similarity between two samples. It is commonly applied in various fields such as image analysis, natural language processing, and information retrieval to evaluate the overlap between predicted and actual outcomes. In the context of machine learning, it is used to evaluate the performance of classification models, particularly in terms of similarity or overlap between sets, and is often compared alongside other metrics like Jaccard, Mcc, F-measure, Precision, Sensitivity, and Specificity."},
