{"mutual_information_mi": "Mutual Information (MI) is a statistical measure used to quantify the amount of information shared between two random variables. In the context of image segmentation evaluation, it assesses the dependency between the segmented image and the ground truth, indicating how well the segmentation algorithm captures the true structures within the image."},
