{"information_theoretic_based_metric": "Information theoretic based metrics are a class of evaluation metrics that apply concepts from information theory, such as entropy and mutual information, to assess the quality of image segmentation. These metrics aim to measure how much information the segmentation result shares with the ground truth, providing insights into the effectiveness of the segmentation process in preserving important image structures and details.|Here is another description: Information theoretic based metrics are a category of evaluation metrics that utilize principles from information theory to assess the quality of image segmentation. These metrics include Mutual Information (MI) and VOI, among others."},
