{"fig_3": "Fig. 3 is a figure in the context that visually represents or details Gelasca\u2019s four basic error types. This figure is used to provide a clear and concise illustration of these error types to aid in the understanding and evaluation of image segmentation results.|Here is another description: Fig. 3 is a visual representation or diagram that serves to convey specific information or concepts. In this context, it is used to illustrate a particular combination of error types as defined by Gelasca."},
{"this_method__is_based_on__human_visual_tolerance": "The phrase \"is based on\" indicates that the method relies on or is founded upon the concept of human visual tolerance to evaluate image segmentation results more accurately."},
{"human_visual_tolerance": "Human visual tolerance refers to the capacity of the human eye to perceive and accept variations or discrepancies in visual stimuli, which in this context is used as a criterion to compensate or penalize errors in image segmentation evaluation."},
