{"border_hole": "The border hole is a type of segmentation error where the boundary of the segmented region does not accurately match the true boundary of the object, resulting in a gap or hole along the border."},
{"purple_rectangle": "The purple rectangle in the context is a visual representation used to illustrate a specific type of segmentation error in image processing. It is one of several colored rectangles that symbolize different error types."},
