{"an_objective_segmentation_evaluation_method_based_on_information_theory": "An objective segmentation evaluation method based on information theory refers to a technique that uses principles from information theory, such as entropy, to assess the quality of image segmentation. This method is objective as it does not rely on subjective human judgment but rather on quantifiable measures derived from information theory."},
{"e__uses__entropy_as_the_basis_for_measuring_the_uniformity_of_pixel_features_within_the_segmentation_region": "The method E employs entropy as a fundamental measure to evaluate the uniformity of pixel features within a segmented region, providing a quantitative assessment of segmentation quality."},
