{"weighted_self_entropy_and_weighted_mutual_entropy_segmentation_evaluation_method": "The weighted self-entropy and weighted mutual entropy segmentation evaluation method is an objective technique proposed by Khan and Bhuiyan in 2011 and 2014 to assess image segmentation quality. It aims to provide a quantitative and unbiased measure of segmentation performance.|Here is another description: The weighted self-entropy and weighted mutual entropy segmentation evaluation method is an objective approach proposed by Khan and Bhuiyan in 2014 and 2011 to measure the heterogeneity of pixels between regions and the homogeneity within regions."},
