{"the_heterogeneity_of_pixels_between_regions_and_the_homogeneity_within_the_region_objectively": "The heterogeneity of pixels between regions refers to the differences in pixel values across different segments of an image, indicating distinct features or objects. Homogeneity within a region signifies uniformity in pixel values, suggesting that the segmented area represents a single, coherent feature or object."},
