{"scale_constraint_assessment_method_qt__normalizes__regional_significance_and_merging_necessity_to_the_equivalent_spectral_distance_of_the_predefined_area": "The predicate \"normalizes\" in this context refers to the process by which the scale constraint assessment method (_Qt_) adjusts and standardizes the measures of regional significance and merging necessity. This normalization is essential to ensure that these measures are comparable and can be effectively used in the evaluation model."},
{"regional_significance_and_merging_necessity_to_the_equivalent_spectral_distance_of_the_predefined_area": "Regional significance and merging necessity are metrics used in the scale constraint assessment method (_Qt_) to describe intra-regional homogeneity and inter-regional heterogeneity, respectively. These metrics are normalized to the equivalent spectral distance of the predefined area to provide a standardized measure for evaluating segmentation quality."},
