{"two_complementary_assessment_methods": "The two complementary assessment methods developed by Karimi et al. (2014) are techniques designed to measure systematic errors in medical image segmentation, such as over-segmentation, under-segmentation, outliers, and overall errors, utilizing statistical techniques and information theory."},
{"benes_and_zitova_2015": "Benes and Zitova (2015) refers to a study conducted by Benes and Zitova in the year 2015, which focused on evaluating image segmentation techniques, particularly in the context of medical imaging.|Here is another description: Benes and Zitova 2015 likely refers to another study or publication by the same or similar authors in the same year. This work could be closely related to the subject, possibly building upon or being a part of the same research project or series of studies."},
