{"f_score_value__obtained_by_combining__precision_and_recall": "The F-score value is obtained by combining Precision and Recall, two fundamental metrics in evaluation methods. This combination aims to provide a more balanced and comprehensive assessment of segmentation performance, addressing the limitations of using either metric alone."},
{"precision_and_recall": "Precision and Recall are critical components in evaluation metrics. Precision measures the accuracy of the segmentation by calculating the ratio of correctly segmented pixels to the total segmented pixels, while Recall measures the completeness by calculating the ratio of correctly segmented pixels to the total ground truth pixels. Together, they form the basis for computing the F-score value."},
