{"a_small_negligible_error": "A small negligible error refers to a minor discrepancy or inaccuracy in the evaluation results provided by _Qp_ and F-score. This error is so small that it does not significantly impact the overall assessment of the segmentation method's performance, making _Qp_ and F-score reliable indicators in this context."},
{"the_results_of_the_two_segmentation_methods": "The results of the two segmentation methods refer to the outcomes obtained from applying mean-shift segmentation and another unspecified method (likely CTM) to an image. These results are being evaluated and compared based on various metrics."},
