{"evaluation_method": "The evaluation method refers to the techniques and criteria used to assess the quality and accuracy of image segmentation results. These methods can be supervised, unsupervised, or analytical, depending on the availability of standard segmentation images and the level of accuracy required.|Here is another description: The evaluation method refers to the techniques and criteria used to assess the quality and effectiveness of image segmentation results. These methods can be supervised, unsupervised, or analytical, depending on the availability of standard segmentation images and the level of accuracy required."},
